From 0a0d3c57b165ba7233704ed51eb9c57fad1cc8e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Try Omarchy Release <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:44:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Recover from an orphaned pacman lock left by an interrupted
 update

An interrupted package transaction can leave /var/lib/pacman/db.lck behind,
and every later update then fails with 'unable to lock database' until it is
removed by hand (issue #90).

Add an early-boot oneshot service that removes the lock only when it cannot
belong to a live transaction: a regular file, no pacman/alpm process running,
no process holding it open, and an mtime that predates the current boot.
Anything ambiguous is left untouched and logged. The recovery ships to
existing disks through the compatibility overlay, so the revision moves to 23.
